<title>SOUTH KOREA: LG Elect issues $75 mln in bonds abroad.</title>
<headline>LG Elect issues $75 mln in bonds abroad.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-06-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>LG Electronics, an affiliate of South Korea's LG Group, has issued $75 million worth of exchangable bonds for LG Semicon in the European market, lead manager LG Securities said on Thursday.</p>
<p>The bond holders would be able to exchange the bonds for LG Semicon's common shares, held by LG Electronics, between August 8, 1997 and November 30, 2007.</p>
<p>LG Electronics currently holds a 46 percent stake in LG Semicon. The bonds represented 1.76 million or 2.468 percent of outstanding LG Semicon shares, an official at LG Securities said.</p>
</text>
